        "original_id": "3210acb8-ea5b-5f41-853d-4260b807c931",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jim Thompson, Theodore H. White\n- Works: Savage Night\n- Roles: author, screenwriter, political journalist, historian, thriller writer\n- Topics: hardboiled crime fiction, wartime reporting from China, U.S. presidential elections\n\nFacts:\n- Jim Thompson was born on September 27, 1906, and he was an American author and screenwriter known for hardboiled crime fiction.\n- Savage Night is a 1953 novel by thriller writer Jim Thompson.\n- Theodore H. White was born on May 6, 1915, and he was an American political journalist and historian known for wartime reporting from China and for accounts of the 1960, 1964, 1968, 1972, 1976, and 1980 presidential elections.\n- Jim Thompson died on April 7, 1977.\n- Theodore H. White died on May 15, 1986.",
